         `reward row` "environmental sciences"          5 "ecotope"                      0 0 1.5 0 1.5 0,
         `reward row` "geography"                       5 "questionnaire"                2.1 (1.2%) 1.4 (0.8%) 3.5 (2%),
         `reward row` "geography"                       5 "geotope"                      0 0 1 0 1 0,
         `reward row` "Land of Israel studies"          5 "questionnaire"                1.05 (0.6%) 2.45 (1.4%) 3.5 (2%),
         `reward row` "Land of Israel studies"          5 "geotope"                      0 0 1 0 1 0

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `chemistry's total percent on` d IS
    IF DATE_SERIAL d AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) THEN 4% ELSE 2%

-- akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p123 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p124 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p125 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p126 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p127 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p128 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p129 The heading "every other elective subject" and the table's column headings.

@ref akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p130 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p131
`any other elective of 5 units` MEANS
    `reward row` "elective subject" 5 "" 2.45 (1.4%) 1.05 (0.6%) 3.5 (2%)

-- The first note under the electives: where a subject divides its exam
-- between external and alternative otherwise than 70%-30% (Chinese,
-- German, the Arab world and Islam, social sciences), the reward is
-- divided in the same proportion. The subject's own external weight is an
-- input.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p132 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p133
GIVEN `subject's reward` IS A NUMBER, `subject's external weight` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the external part of the reward` `subject's reward` `subject's external weight` IS
    `subject's reward` TIMES `subject's external weight`

GIVEN `subject's reward` IS A NUMBER, `subject's external weight` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the alternative part of the reward` `subject's reward` `subject's external weight` IS
    `subject's reward` TIMES (1 MINUS `subject's external weight`)

-- The second note: where an elective has more than one external exam event
-- or more than one alternative-assessment event, the part's reward is
-- divided accordingly (religious Bible, for instance) — read, as the
-- compulsory table's own notes say for those subjects, as equally between
-- the events.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p134 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p135
GIVEN `part's reward` IS A NUMBER, events IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an elective part's reward per event` `part's reward` events IS
    `the reward per event` `part's reward` events

-- The third note: where a technological elective is split into 3 + 2
-- units, the rewards are divided accordingly — by the units.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p136
GIVEN `subject's reward` IS A NUMBER, `units of the part` IS A NUMBER, `units of the subject` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the reward of a technological part` `subject's reward` `units of the part` `units of the subject` IS
    `subject's reward` TIMES `units of the part` DIVIDED BY `units of the subject`

§§ `תכניות הבגרויות הגמישה`

-- akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p137 The heading "the flexible matriculation programmes".

-- p138-p143: controlled performance tasks are those the circular of
-- 4.3.2024 defines, done and assessed in the Ministry's dedicated online
-- system; the links lead to that circular and to the programme's site.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p138 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p139 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p140 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p141 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p142 akn:hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p143
GIVEN `defined by the circular of 4.3.2024` IS A BOOLEAN, `done and assessed in the Ministry's system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a controlled performance task` `defined by the circular of 4.3.2024` `done and assessed in the Ministry's system` IF
    `defined by the circular of 4.3.2024` AND `done and assessed in the Ministry's system`

-- akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p2 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p3 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p4 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p5 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p6 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p7 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p8 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p9 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p10 The table's column headings: the reward outside the flexible outline (external 70%, alternative 30%, total) and in it (performance tasks "**35%", external 35%, alternative 30%, total), in hours and percent.
-- akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p23 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p24 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p25 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p26 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p27 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p28 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p29 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p30 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p31 The column headings repeated at the top of the next page.
-- akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p48 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p49 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p50 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p51 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p52 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p53 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p54 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p55 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p56 The column headings repeated at the top of the next page.

@desc One printed row of the flexible programme's table: the reward outside the flexible outline (the pre-change outline) and in it, in weekly hours and percent.
DECLARE `flexible row` HAS
    `flexible subject`                 IS A STRING
    `flexible units`                   IS A NUMBER
    `pre-change external hours`        IS A NUMBER
    `pre-change external percent`      IS A NUMBER
    `pre-change alternative hours`     IS A NUMBER
    `pre-change alternative percent`   IS A NUMBER
    `pre-change total hours`           IS A NUMBER
    `pre-change total percent`         IS A NUMBER
    `tasks hours`                      IS A NUMBER
    `tasks percent`                    IS A NUMBER
    `flexible external hours`          IS A NUMBER
    `flexible external percent`        IS A NUMBER
    `flexible alternative hours`       IS A NUMBER
    `flexible alternative percent`     IS A NUMBER
    `flexible total hours`             IS A NUMBER
    `flexible total percent`           IS A NUMBER

GIVEN r IS A `flexible row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the flexible row adds up` r IF
        r's `tasks hours` PLUS r's `flexible external hours` PLUS r's `flexible alternative hours` EQUALS r's `flexible total hours`
    AND r's `tasks percent` PLUS r's `flexible external percent` PLUS r's `flexible alternative percent` EQUALS r's `flexible total percent`

-- The header's split of the flexible reward: tasks 35%, external 35%,
-- alternative 30%.
GIVEN r IS A `flexible row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row follows the header's 35-35-30 split` r IF
        r's `tasks hours` EQUALS 35% TIMES r's `flexible total hours`
    AND r's `flexible external hours` EQUALS 35% TIMES r's `flexible total hours`
    AND r's `flexible alternative hours` EQUALS 30% TIMES r's `flexible total hours`

-- The rows, in the printed order. The notes: two controlled tasks (one in
-- the one-unit subjects); where each task is submitted in a different
-- school year, the tasks' reward is divided between them (ג above).
-- Civics' performance task does not exist in the flexible outline.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p11 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p12 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p13 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p14 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p15 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p16 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p17 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p18 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p19 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p20 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p21 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p22 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p32 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p33 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p34 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p39 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p40 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p41 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p42 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p43 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p44 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p45 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p46 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p47 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p57 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p58 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p59 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p60 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/t1 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p61
`the flexible programme rows` MEANS
    LIST `flexible row` "Bible, state"          2 1.05 (1.4%) 0.45 (0.6%) 1.5 (2%)  0.525 (0.7%) 0.525 (0.7%) 0.45 (0.6%) 1.5 (2%),
         `flexible row` "literature, state"     2 1.05 (1.4%) 0.45 (0.6%) 1.5 (2%)  0.525 (0.7%) 0.525 (0.7%) 0.45 (0.6%) 1.5 (2%),
         `flexible row` "history"               2 1.05 (1.4%) 0.45 (0.6%) 1.5 (2%)  0.525 (0.7%) 0.525 (0.7%) 0.45 (0.6%) 1.5 (2%),
         `flexible row` "civics"                2 1.5  (2%)   0    0    1.5 (2%)  0.525 (0.7%) 0.525 (0.7%) 0.45 (0.6%) 1.5 (2%),
         `flexible row` "Bible, religious"      3 1.4  (1.4%) 0.6  (0.6%) 2   (2%)  0.7   (0.7%) 0.7   (0.7%) 0.6  (0.6%) 2   (2%),
         `flexible row` "Oral Torah, religious" 3 1.4  (1.4%) 0.6  (0.6%) 2   (2%)  0.7   (0.7%) 0.7   (0.7%) 0.6  (0.6%) 2   (2%),
         `flexible row` "Judaism, Haredi"       3 0.8  (0.8%) 1.2  (1.2%) 2   (2%)  0.7   (0.7%) 0.7   (0.7%) 0.6  (0.6%) 2   (2%),
         `flexible row` "Bible, Haredi"         3 0.8  (0.8%) 1.2  (1.2%) 2   (2%)  0.7   (0.7%) 0.7   (0.7%) 0.6  (0.6%) 2   (2%),
         `flexible row` "literature, religious" 1 0.7  (1.4%) 0.3  (0.6%) 1   (2%)  0.2   (0.4%) 0.5   (1%)   0.3  (0.6%) 1   (2%),
         `flexible row` "Jewish thought, religious" 1 0.7 (1.4%) 0.3 (0.6%) 1 (2%)  0.2   (0.4%) 0.5   (1%)   0.3  (0.6%) 1   (2%),
         `flexible row` "Druze culture and heritage / Islam / Christianity" 1 0.7 (1.4%) 0.3 (0.6%) 1 (2%) 0.2 (0.4%) 0.5 (1%) 0.3 (0.6%) 1 (2%)

-- Civics' performance task: 0.4 hour outside the flexible outline (in the
-- alternative column), none in it.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p35 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p36 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p37 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p38
GIVEN `in the flexible outline` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `civics performance-task hours` `in the flexible outline` IS
    IF `in the flexible outline` THEN 0 ELSE 0.4

§§ `תכנית האקדמיזציה`

-- akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p62 The heading "the academisation programme".

@desc One printed row of the academisation table: a part of a subject, its units, and its reward in weekly hours and percent for the external exam and the alternative assessment, with the subject's total.
DECLARE `academisation row` HAS
    `academisation subject`             IS A STRING
    `academisation subject units`       IS A NUMBER
    `part of the subject`               IS A STRING
    `part units`                        IS A NUMBER
    `part external hours`               IS A NUMBER
    `part external percent`             IS A NUMBER
    `part alternative hours`            IS A NUMBER
    `part alternative percent`          IS A NUMBER
    `subject total hours`               IS A NUMBER
    `subject total percent`             IS A NUMBER

-- p63-p64: where some of a subject's units are done in the academisation
-- programme, the reward for the external exam (about 70% of the subject's
-- reward) is divided between the units done in the programme and those
-- done outside it, by the number of units in each, in proportion to the
-- subject's total units; each share is given in the year the class sits
-- the programme's final exam or the matriculation exam outside it. The
-- alternative assessment's reward (about 30%) is unchanged.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p63 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p64
GIVEN `external reward` IS A NUMBER, `academisation units` IS A NUMBER, `subject units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the academisation share as the rule states it` `external reward` `academisation units` `subject units` IS
    `external reward` TIMES `academisation units` DIVIDED BY `subject units`

GIVEN `external reward` IS A NUMBER, `academisation units` IS A NUMBER, `subject units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the external share left as the rule states it` `external reward` `academisation units` `subject units` IS
    `external reward` MINUS `the academisation share as the rule states it` `external reward` `academisation units` `subject units`

-- The share the worked example and the table give: the subject's WHOLE
-- reward in proportion to the units, taken out of the external part
-- (F-2024-25_tashpah_10-a). This file follows the circular's own example.
GIVEN `subject reward` IS A NUMBER, `academisation units` IS A NUMBER, `subject units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the academisation share as the example computes it` `subject reward` `academisation units` `subject units` IS
    `subject reward` TIMES `academisation units` DIVIDED BY `subject units`

-- The worked example: a 5-unit subject rewarded 3.5 hours and 2%, one unit
-- in the programme; of the external part (2.45 hours and 1.4%), 0.7 hour
-- and 0.4% for the programme's final exam and 1.75 hours and 1% for the
-- matriculation exam; the alternative part stays 1.05 hours + 0.6%.
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p65 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p66 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p67 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p68 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p69
`the example's split` MEANS
    LIST 0.7, 0.4%, 1.75, 1%, 1.05, 0.6%

-- The table: an elective of 5 units (one in the programme — the number of
-- units in it may vary between electives, and the reward with it) and
-- literature of 2 units (external 50%, alternative 50%).
@ref akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p70 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p71 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p72 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p73 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p74 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p75 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p76 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p77 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p78 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p79 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p80 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p81 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p82 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p83 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p84 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p85 akn:hc_1__hc_2__para_d/p86
`the academisation table` MEANS
    LIST `academisation row` "elective subject" 5 "in the academisation programme"            1 0.7  (0.4%) 0    0    3.5 (2%),
         `academisation row` "elective subject" 5 "external questionnaire and alternative"   4 1.75 (1%)   1.05 (0.6%) 3.5 (2%),
         `academisation row` "literature"       2 "in the academisation programme"            1 0.75 (1%)   0    0    1.5 (2%),
         `academisation row` "literature"       2 "alternative assessment"                    1 0    0    0.75 (1%)   1.5 (2%)

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples and checks.

-- Every subject row adds up: external + alternative = total, in hours and
-- in percent (the English oral rows print no total and are left out).
#ASSERT all `the row adds up` `the mathematics rows`
#ASSERT all `the row adds up` (filter (GIVEN r YIELD NOT `is an oral exam` (r's `questionnaire`)) `the English rows`)
#ASSERT all `the row adds up` `the other compulsory rows`
#ASSERT all `the row adds up` `the language rows`
#ASSERT `the row adds up` `language and expression in the project`
#ASSERT all `the row adds up` `the special elective rows`
#ASSERT `the row adds up` `any other elective of 5 units`
#ASSERT all `the flexible row adds up` `the flexible programme rows`

-- The 70-30 split of the general elective, and geography's 60-40.
#ASSERT `the external part of the reward` 3.5 (70%) EQUALS 2.45
#ASSERT `the external part of the reward` 3.5 (60%) EQUALS 2.1

-- Class size: a class of 8 receives half the table's reward.
#ASSERT `the reward for the class` 3.5 8 EQUALS 1.75
#ASSERT `the reward for the class` 3.5 12 EQUALS 3.5
#ASSERT `the reward for the class` 3.5 4 EQUALS 0.875
#ASSERT `does not entitle the teacher to the preparation reward` `internal assessment`
#ASSERT `the tasks' reward given this year` 0.525 1 2 EQUALS 0.2625
#ASSERT `chemistry's total percent on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) EQUALS 4%

-- The academisation table reproduces the example's split.
#ASSERT `the academisation share as the example computes it` 3.5 1 5 EQUALS 0.7
#ASSERT `the academisation share as the example computes it` (2%) 1 5 EQUALS 0.4%
#ASSERT 2.45 MINUS `the academisation share as the example computes it` 3.5 1 5 EQUALS 1.75
#ASSERT `the academisation share as the example computes it` 1.5 1 2 EQUALS 0.75

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_10-a: the rule divides the EXTERNAL part by the units
-- and gives the programme's unit 2.45 × 1/5 = 0.49 hour (0.28%); the
-- circular's example and table give it 0.7 hour (0.4%).
`the academisation rule and its example disagree` MEANS
        `the academisation share as the rule states it` 2.45 1 5 EQUALS 0.49
    AND `the academisation share as the rule states it` (1.4%) 1 5 EQUALS 0.28%
    AND NOT `the academisation share as the rule states it` 2.45 1 5 EQUALS 0.7
#ASSERT `the academisation rule and its example disagree`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_10-b: the one-unit rows of the flexible table do not
-- follow the 35-35-30 split their header states (tasks 0.2 of 1 hour, 20%;
-- external 0.5, 50%), while every row of two or three units does.
`the one-unit flexible rows leave the header's split` MEANS
        all (GIVEN r YIELD NOT `the row follows the header's 35-35-30 split` r)
            (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `flexible units` EQUALS 1) `the flexible programme rows`)
    AND all `the row follows the header's 35-35-30 split`
            (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `flexible units` GREATER THAN 1) `the flexible programme rows`)
#ASSERT `the one-unit flexible rows leave the header's split`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_10-c: every reward is printed both in weekly hours and
-- in percent, and the circular never says which teacher is paid which.
`the circular says who is paid in hours and who in percent` MEANS FALSE

`every reward is given in two units` MEANS
        all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `total hours` GREATER THAN 0 AND r's `total percent` GREATER THAN 0)
            (append `the mathematics rows` `the language rows`)
    AND NOT `the circular says who is paid in hours and who in percent`
#ASSERT `every reward is given in two units`
